<title>FRANCE: TABLE - FRENCH BUDGET DEFICIT 202.3 BLN FFR IN H1.</title>
<headline>TABLE - FRENCH BUDGET DEFICIT 202.3 BLN FFR IN H1.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French budget deficit at the end of June stood at 202.3 billion francs, down 24.0 billion from 226.3 billion francs a year earlier, the finance ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Cumulative net tax receipts stood at 713.4 billion francs at end June, up 2.4 percent from 696.4 billion francs for the same period a year earlier, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Cumulative general budget revenues were up 2.2 percent at 671.2 billion francs, it said.</p>
<p>General budget spending was down 0.7 percent at end June at 821.6 billion francs, over the same period a year earlier.  </p>
<p> (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1997 year forecast):</p>
<p> REVENUES			end Jun 97  Jun 96  pct	1997</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		 713.4    696.4   2.4    1,395.3</p>
<p>  of which: -- income tax     169.7    170.2  -0.3	291.8</p>
<p>  -- net company tax	     82.3     77.5   6.2	144.8</p>
<p>  -- petrol duties		 70.9     70.2   1.0	151.9</p>
<p>  -- net Value Added Tax	304.5    298.7   1.9	635.2</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		 86.0     79.8   7.8	171.6</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		  56.0     51.8   8.1	155.1</p>
<p> Local authority, EU charges -129.6   -125.7   3.1     -253.9</p>
<p> General budget receipts	671.2    656.9   2.2    1,296.5</p>
